# gitleaks — findings reviewed and accepted, pinned by FINGERPRINT.
#
# ⚠️ READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A LINE.
#
# A fingerprint is `commit:path:rule:line`. Pinning one accepts EXACTLY that
# finding at EXACTLY that point in history — it does NOT blind the scanner to the
# file, the rule, or any future secret pasted into the same place. That precision
# is the whole reason this file is used instead of a `paths` entry in
# `.gitleaks.toml`: excluding a path would make the scanner permanently silent
# about it, which is how a real secret eventually ships.
#
# The same reasoning as `desktop/.cargo/audit.toml`: an accepted finding belongs
# in the repository with a justification, where it can be reviewed in a diff — not
# hidden behind a CI flag, and not silenced by widening a rule.
#
# ⛔ NOTHING that is actually secret goes here. If a real credential is ever
# committed, the answer is rotation and history rewriting — see the "gitleaks
# fired" rotation runbook in docs/sprint-72h.md.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-07-30. Every entry below was opened and read, not assumed.

