# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE SAME FOUR FINDINGS AGAIN, IN NO-GIT FORM.
#
# A fingerprint from a HISTORY scan is `commit:path:rule:line`. A fingerprint
# from a `--no-git` scan of a working tree has no commit, so it is just
# `path:rule:line` — and the entries above therefore DO NOT MATCH IT.
# `scripts/gate.sh` runs both (history, matching CI; and the working tree,
# because the history scan provably cannot see a secret you have not committed
# yet), so both spellings are needed or the gate reports four permanent leaks.
#
# ⚠️ Line numbers here track the CURRENT file, not the commit that introduced
# the finding — extension/manifest.json has moved from line 12 to line 14 — so
# these will need updating when the surrounding code moves. If one goes stale
# the gate fails LOUDLY, which is the right failure direction.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
desktop/core/src/recovery.rs:generic-api-key:616
desktop/core/src/recovery.rs:generic-api-key:624
extension/manifest.json:generic-api-key:14
